OpenStreetMap — schools, hospitals and transit stops
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Loaded on demand by `python -m ingestion osm` from the Overpass API.
Data © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database License
(ODbL) 1.0: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/
  - Attribution is required wherever the data is shown. The UI displays
    "© OpenStreetMap contributors" on maps and neighbourhood panels.
  - If you publicly distribute a database derived from OSM data (for example
    a dump of the house_schools / house_bus_stops tables), that database must
    be offered under the ODbL. Serving it through the application is not
    distribution of the database.
  - Use the public Overpass instance sparingly (the loader runs one query per
    city, weekly) or self-host one: https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Overpass_API

Map tiles are served by openstreetmap.org and subject to the OSM Tile Usage
Policy: https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles/ — heavy or
commercial use requires your own tile source.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Municipal, provincial and federal open data — `python -m ingestion opendata`
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The loaders in services/ingestion-worker/ingestion/opendata fetch public data
under each publisher's open licence. Each load is recorded in od_load_log with
its licence and required attribution, and the UI lists them (/api/v1/data-sources).
  - City of Toronto, City of Vancouver, City of Calgary, City of Ottawa:
    Open Government Licence (municipal variants) — "Contains information
    licensed under the Open Government Licence – <City>".
  - City of Edmonton: Open Data Terms of Use.
  - Ville de Montréal: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0.
  - Statistics Canada (Census 2021, data tables): Statistics Canada Open
    Licence — "Source: Statistics Canada".
  - Bank of Canada (Valet API): attribution to the Bank of Canada required.
  - Transit agencies (TTC, TransLink, Calgary Transit, ETS, OC Transpo, STM):
    each agency's GTFS terms of use.
  - Toronto Police Service Public Safety Data Portal: its open data licence.
    Only per-neighbourhood counts are stored, not incident records.
Assessment-roll records describe real properties. They are public, but the app
shows them only as property facts (value, year built, tax); it does not attach
owner information, which these datasets do not contain.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Rent benchmarks — data/reference/rent_benchmarks.csv
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The file shipped in this repository contains PLACEHOLDER values that
approximate the CMHC Rental Market Survey format. They are not official
statistics. Replace them with figures from the Canada Mortgage and Housing
Corporation (https://www.cmhc-schl.gc.ca/) and follow CMHC's terms of use for
that data, including its attribution requirements.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Synthetic demo listings
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Listings created by `python -m ingestion seed` are generated by code in this
repository (MIT). They are fictitious: prices, sizes and history are not
market data. Neighbourhood names and approximate centroids are real places,
used only to make the demo map legible. Every synthetic listing is stored with
is_synthetic = 1 and must be labelled as such in any interface.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Listing feeds
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NeighborIQ does not scrape MLS® or REALTOR.ca; their terms prohibit it.
Real listings must come from a source you are licensed to use (for example
CREA's Data Distribution Facility through a member brokerage) and must be
displayed according to that licence. MLS® and REALTOR® are trademarks of The
Canadian Real Estate Association.
